<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Facial Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A walled collection of pus within facial soft tissues — well-defined red swelling that may feel fluid-filled. Requires surgical drainage. See our <a href="facial-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">facial abscess treatment</a> page.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Dental Infection Spread</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Cheek swelling from a tooth or gum infection. Typically starts near a specific tooth and spreads to facial spaces, causing cheek or jawline redness.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Infected Skin Cyst</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Sebaceous or epidermal cysts on the face commonly become infected — red, swollen, and tender. May need antibiotic therapy or excision.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Allergic Reaction / Angioedema</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Sudden lip or facial swelling from an allergic trigger — may involve the tongue and airway. Requires epinephrine and antihistamine therapy urgently.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Insect Bite with Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bug bites on the face that become secondarily infected with bacteria produce significant redness and swelling. May require antibiotics and drainage.</p></div>
